MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_001: Father...isn't here. Maybe I should ask someone...\nOh?! M-Mom?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_002: Mu? Actually, this is a good chance to talk. Don't\nworry—I'm not going to start a fight.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_003: Aww...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_004: After we talked, I thought about what I was like at\nyour age. I used to give your grandparents hell.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_005: Wha?! You did?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_006: You might be surprised to hear it, but your aunt and I\nwere known as the local beauties.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_007: Your grandparents did their very best to raise\nus right.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_008: And you know your aunt. She was very obedient.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_009: But me... Well, I was always fighting with the boys.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_010: I didn't want a boyfriend. I wanted a sword. So I\nleft home.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_011: I wanted to find my own path, not the one that was\nset out for me by my parents.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_012: So...so...WHY do you keep trying to control me?!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_013: You picked your own path and you succeeded! You\ngot to be the famous "Mikaela Redblade"!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_014: You've got it all wrong. I didn't succeed at anything.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_015: What do you mean?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_016: A mercenary has a hard life, Mu.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_017: All you're left with after the job is some money and\nyour life. And the sensation of taking someone else's.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_018: It might be different if it were a just cause, like the\ntemple knights.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_019: For mercenaries, there are just two choices. Let the\nbattlefield rule your soul and fight till you die...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_020: or lose your nerve and call it quits. Everyone I know\nchose one or the other.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_021: If you're famous, it's a hollow kind of fame. All it gets\nyou is a bunch of jobs that are, well, meaningless.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_022: Maybe I'm making it sound worse than it is. I've\nchosen my path, and I'll see it through.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_023: Still, I often think that if I'd just listened to your\ngrandparents, I'd have had a life like your aunt's.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_024: That's why you want me to listen to you? Look, you\nmay be a failure, but that doesn't mean I'll be one!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_025: Mu! We're not done here! Damn, I've made a mess\nof it. Again. What now?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_026: Haaah... Haaah... So that's how Mom thinks\nof herself? 
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_C_027: But I'm not her! How do I make her understand that?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_001: I'm finally getting close to making back the money.\nThank the war, I guess.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_002: I still haven't been able to have a conversation with\nMu, and the temples are in chaos.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_003: Mom...I'd like to talk to you. Is now a good time?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_004: Mu? Yes, sure. We can chat. Just so you know,\nI don't have all the money yet.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_005: About that. I've thought about studying magic. I even\nfound that great mage your contact told you about.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_006: Really? That's such good news! I heard he'd retired,\nso nice work tracking him down!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_007: I know I said I don't have the money quite yet, but\nI've saved up most of it. When the war's over...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_008: No, it's fine. I've decided not to work for the temple.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_009: What? Why? This is a huge mistake!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_010: Mom, listen... That mage told me he doesn't need any\nmoney from you to take me on as an apprentice.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_011: That's not right! Nothing you're saying is. The\nperson I met told me just what to do...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_012: That's what I'm trying to tell you... You shouldn't\ntrust that person. They were lying to you.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_013: Lying to me? But if the mage doesn't want money,\nwhy don't you plan to join the temple anymore?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_014: You're so talented with magic!
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_015: Not really. In all honesty, I don't think I have any\nkind of unusual talent. I'm just...normal.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_016: Also, there's something else I want to do. Something\nthat doesn't involve working for the temple.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_017: Wait. What is this now?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_018: I can't...live the life you want me to, Mom. I'm sorry.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_019: I... I see. What have I been doing all this time?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_020: I got everything turned around. All I ended up doing\nwas pushing you away. I really am a failure.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_021: "Turned around"? What do you mean?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_022: Do you remember that day we talked at the tavern?\nI told you I hadn't succeeded at all.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_023: The only good thing I ever did was having you. You\nmade me happy.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_024: When the gods gave me you, I quit being a\nmercenary and learned how to be a mom.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_025: No matter how hard things got, I had my love for\nyou. That made it all worthwhile.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_026: All I wanted to do was make you happy. That would\ngive my life meaning, I thought.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_027: Mom...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_028: When you read that tome and healed someone with\nyour cooking, I thought you'd found your calling.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_029: My daughter can use magic! Surely, Smyrnos will see\nhow talented she is.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_030: I was wrong. And in the end I didn't make you happy\nat all. I made you miserable.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_031: I'm sorry, Mu. I'm so sorry. I'm such a fool. *sob*
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_032: Don't cry, Mom. And don't apologize. I always knew\nthat everything you did, you did for me.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_033: And yeah, you may have gotten some things wrong,\nbut you didn't fail.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_034: I mean, I love having a mom who's a fearsome\nbrawler and mercenary. I'm happy I'm your daughter.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_035: Ah...
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_036: I grew up watching you live your life your way. I just\nwant you to enjoy watching me live mine. Please?
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_037: OK, Mu. I will.
MID_SE_Mic_Moo_B_038: When did you grow into such a strong woman?\nI wonder where you get it from. Heh.